---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const locale = 'en';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Reporting & Management Insight — Dashboards, Analytics, BSC"
  description="Real-time dashboards, management reports, drill-down analytics, AI-powered commentary, strategic KPI tracking, and balanced scorecard. Part of Kraal Code ERP."
  locale={locale}
  canonicalUrl="https://kraalcode.com/en/capabilities/reporting/"
>
  <section class="page-hero section--warm">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/en/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/en/capabilities/">Capabilities</a></li><li aria-current="page">Reporting & Management Insight</li></ol></nav>
      <h1>Reporting & Management Insight</h1>
      <p class="page-hero-subtext">Every module feeds one reporting layer. Real-time dashboards, financial statements, operational reports, and strategic KPIs — all from the same data.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container container--narrow">
    <h2>Who this is for</h2>
    <p>CEOs, directors, department heads, and anyone who needs to see what is happening across the organisation — without waiting for month-end reports or asking someone to run a query.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section section--warm"><div class="container">
    <h2>What you can do</h2>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Executive Dashboard</h3><p>Today's sales, monthly performance with achievement bars, low stock alerts, gross margin, active customers, and 12-month trend charts. The first screen a managing director sees.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Accounting Dashboard</h3><p>Total assets, liabilities, equity, and net profit at a glance. Current ratio, debt-to-equity, and profit margin with Healthy/Fair/Weak indicators. Trial balance status.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Sales Manager Dashboard</h3><p>Sales performance by rep, territory, and product. Pipeline visibility. Achievement against targets. Top customers and overdue accounts.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Store Dashboard</h3><p>Active stores, total stock value, low stock items, inventory by location with utilisation bars, pending transfers, and expiring batches with urgency badges.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Procurement Dashboard</h3><p>Open purchase requests, open POs, GRNs today, pending invoices, AP total with overdue aging, and quick actions for procurement officers.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>KPI Dashboard</h3><p>Strategic KPIs with targets and actuals. Track performance across financial, customer, internal process, and learning perspectives. Linked to the balanced scorecard.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Compliance Dashboard</h3><p>Monitor compliance status across the organisation. Track audit findings, corrective actions, and regulatory requirements. Generate compliance reports for boards and regulators.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Financial Statements</h3><p>Profit and loss, balance sheet, cash flow statement, and trial balance. Departmental and consolidated views. Export to PDF or Excel. Configurable reporting periods.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container container--narrow">
    <h2>How it connects</h2>
    <p>Reporting is not a separate module — it is the lens through which every other module is visible. Every dashboard pulls from the same live data:</p>
    <ul class="connection-list">
      <li><strong>Accounting</strong> → financial statements, budgets, trial balance</li>
      <li><strong>Sales</strong> → sales trends, customer analytics, agent performance</li>
      <li><strong>Inventory</strong> → stock levels, valuation, movement history</li>
      <li><strong>Procurement</strong> → spend analysis, vendor performance, AP aging</li>
      <li><strong>HR</strong> → headcount, payroll costs, leave balances</li>
      <li><strong>Manufacturing</strong> → production efficiency, yield, QC statistics</li>
      <li><strong>Strategy & BSC</strong> → strategic objectives, KPIs, departmental workplans</li>
    </ul>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section section--warm"><div class="container">
    <h2>See it in action</h2>
    <p class="screenshot-intro">Screenshots from the live Kraal Code system — coming soon.</p>
    <div class="screenshot-grid">
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">Executive Dashboard</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">KPI Dashboard</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">Compliance Dashboard</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">Strategic Plan</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section--dark section"><div class="container text-center">
    <h2>See reporting in action</h2><p>Request a demonstration tailored to your management reporting needs.</p>
    <a href="/en/contact/" class="btn btn--inverse">Request a Demonstration →</a>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero{padding:var(--kc-space-20) 0 var(--kc-space-12)}.page-hero h1{font-size:var(--kc-text-4xl);max-width:700px}.page-hero-subtext{font-size:var(--kc-text-lg);color:var(--kc-text-secondary);max-width:60ch;margin-top:var(--kc-space-4)}.breadcrumb ol{list-style:none;padding:0;display:flex;gap:var(--kc-space-2);font-size:var(--kc-text-sm);color:var(--kc-text-tertiary);margin-bottom:var(--kc-space-6)}.breadcrumb a{color:var(--kc-teal);text-decoration:none}.breadcrumb li:not(:last-child)::after{content:'/';margin-left:var(--kc-space-2);color:var(--kc-text-tertiary)}.container--narrow{max-width:var(--kc-container-narrow)}.feature-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:var(--kc-space-6);margin-top:var(--kc-space-8)}.feature-card{padding:var(--kc-space-6);background:var(--kc-surface-light);border:1px solid var(--kc-border-subtle);border-radius:var(--kc-radius-lg)}.feature-card h3{font-size:var(--kc-text-lg);font-family:var(--kc-font-body);font-weight:var(--kc-weight-semibold);margin-bottom:var(--kc-space-2)}.feature-card p{font-size:var(--kc-text-sm);color:var(--kc-text-secondary)}.connection-list{margin-top:var(--kc-space-4)}.connection-list li{margin-bottom:var(--kc-space-3);font-size:var(--kc-text-base);color:var(--kc-text-secondary)}.connection-list strong{color:var(--kc-text-primary)}.screenshot-intro{color:var(--kc-text-secondary);margin-bottom:var(--kc-space-6)}.screenshot-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:var(--kc-space-6)}.screenshot-placeholder{aspect-ratio:16/10;background:var(--kc-surface-warm);border:2px dashed var(--kc-border);border-radius:var(--kc-radius-lg);display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:var(--kc-space-2)}.screenshot-label{font-weight:var(--kc-weight-semibold);color:var(--kc-text-primary)}.screenshot-note{font-size:var(--kc-text-sm);color:var(--kc-text-tertiary)}.btn--inverse{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:var(--kc-space-4) var(--kc-space-8);font-weight:var(--kc-weight-semibold);font-size:var(--kc-text-base);border-radius:var(--kc-radius-lg);background:transparent;color:var(--kc-text-inverse);border:2px solid var(--kc-teal-light);transition:all var(--kc-transition-fast);text-decoration:none;margin-top:var(--kc-space-6)}.btn--inverse:hover{background:var(--kc-teal);border-color:var(--kc-teal)}@media(max-width:768px){.page-hero h1{font-size:var(--kc-text-3xl)}.feature-grid,.screenshot-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
